1
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,390
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:09,790
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,070
♪Set reality aside♪

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,390
♪Follow your heart♪

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,750
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,230
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,110
♪Just be a little braver♪

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,870
♪Come closer, come closer♪

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:23,950
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

10
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,070
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,790
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,820
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,700
(Cui Kaiyi & Cao Yiheng Mutual Date)

14
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,600
This courtyard is all enclosed
with brick walls.

15
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,440
It has such a nice

16
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,240
atmosphere.

17
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,640
Did you ever live somewhere like this
as a kid?

18
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:52,040
I stayed at my grandma's as a kid,

19
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:53,200
but not for long.

20
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:55,520
I did too when I was little.

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:56,480
What?

22
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:58,040
I lived in a place like this
for quite a few years.

23
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,280
- Where?
- With these kinds of bricks.

24
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,920
My home.

25
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,520
It has a nice vibe.

26
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:05,320
I think so too.

27
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,200
Thanks.

28
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,200
Thank you.

29
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:08,480
Let's dig in.

30
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,240
Looks good.

31
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,920
Should I move it a little closer?

32
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:15,000
It's okay.
I'll just sit a little closer to you.

33
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:16,520
Here.

34
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,640
(Asking)
What flavor do you want?

35
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:20,760
Anything is fine.

36
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,080
I'll get you a light green one.

37
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,480
And I'll get a dark green one.

38
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:26,080
We're going with green today.

39
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,640
Thank you.

40
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:31,600
Okay, let's dig in.

41
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,360
Do you want some shrimp?

42
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,400
I'll get one for you.

43
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:35,680
Sure.

44
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,040
(Helping serve the food)
Thanks.

45
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,240
That's huge.

46
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,520
Yeah, they're all this big.

47
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,200
It's pretty good.

48
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,160
This is really good.

49
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:49,680
Yeah, it's good.

50
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,280
Focus on eating.

51
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:58,080
(Teasing)
Go at your usual pace.

52
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,640
What?

53
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:02,000
I'm actually holding back lately.

54
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:02,920
Do you think all this food

55
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,360
(Keep teasing)
is enough for us?

56
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,240
Isn't all this enough?

57
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,040
How much more do you want?

58
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:08,800
More.

59
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:09,840
Ten more dishes.

60
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,740
(Joking)
Make me one of everything.

61
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,960
So, are you happy today?

62
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,480
Of course I am.

63
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,440
What about you?

64
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:21,920
I'm happy.

65
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,040
I hope you'll tell me
when something's bothering you.

66
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:29,160
I'm a little

67
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:32,480
high-maintenance emotionally.

68
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,520
What do you think?

69
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,920
I think when either of us
is feeling something,

70
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,560
we should just tell each other.

71
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,360
That's what
a healthy relationship looks like.

72
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,000
Yeah.

73
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,880
And I'm the kind of person

74
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:49,920
who needs you
to share your feelings with me.

75
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,200
It makes me feel needed.

76
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:53,920
You know what I mean?

77
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:54,240
Like...

78
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,000
I do.

79
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,840
I feel the same way.

80
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,360
When you open up to me
about your feelings,

81
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,880
it means you trust me.

82
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,520
It's about trusting each other.

83
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,440
I was thinking about it yesterday.

84
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:11,080
We have different personalities,

85
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,280
and maybe the way we think

86
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,440
is a little different.

87
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,840
But I actually think
that's a good thing.

88
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,480
What do you think?

89
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,520
It makes us

90
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,640
complementary.

91
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,600
Is being complementary good or bad?

92
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,920
Of course it's good.

93
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,200
I think I'm pretty
high-maintenance emotionally

94
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,600
because

95
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,040
encouragement

96
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,320
from others

97
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:37,160
motivates me to keep learning
and moving forward.

98
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:41,320
Maybe I can slowly pass on...

99
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,080
What?

100
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:44,480
My calm and steady attitude

101
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,000
toward work to you.

102
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,720
Aren't you supposed
to encourage me more?

103
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,720
I just want you
to take your time and not rush.

104
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,760
When you draw,

105
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,120
do you feel more relaxed

106
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:59,640
or stressed?

107
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:01,840
I think

108
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,240
I'm more relaxed.

109
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:03,760
Because

110
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:09,880
I think stress comes
from being too rational.

111
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,080
In a way,

112
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,240
drawing

113
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,360
is also a way

114
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,000
to relieve stress.

115
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:18,200
For example,
when you're drawing on paper,

116
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:22,360
you can just draw whatever you want.

117
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,320
It's basically

118
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,600
a way to release your stress.

119
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,800
When I come back stressed from work,

120
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,520
I'll just find you and draw with you.

121
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,020
(Laughs)
Sure.

122
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,320
We can draw together.

123
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,920
Alright, let's head back.

124
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,720
Let's go.

125
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,080
Why doesn't it come with a manual?

126
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:48,090
(Checking the polaroid)
I'm the instruction manual expert.

127
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,000
Can this be pressed?

128
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,880
This can flip open.

129
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,040
It can?

130
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:55,840
I feel like this can flip open.

131
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:00,480
So that's how it is.

132
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,200
Yeah.

133
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,680
That's how you take the picture.

134
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,920
You can see the image through here.

135
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,440
The image lets you see
how the shot is framed.

136
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,240
I can take some good photos of you now.

137
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:11,960
Okay.

138
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:17,720
There is a manual?

139
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:20,600
It's on the side,
but it's covered by that paper.

140
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,960
A little instruction manual.

141
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:26,920
I got it.

142
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,400
(Asking)
Did you buy the bag separately?

143
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,280
No, it came as a set.

144
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,400
With this box.

145
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,720
You bought the box separately?

146
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,320
No, the box and the bag came as a set.

147
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:40,600
This isn't part of the set, right?

148
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,400
Right.

149
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,960
That's what I mean.

150
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:44,560
So you bought it separately?

151
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,480
It came with this one.

152
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:47,240
It came with that one.

153
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:49,280
You're confusing me.

154
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,520
The box and the bag are a set.

155
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,040
Right.

156
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,280
The bag and the box are a set.

157
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:54,960
Right.

158
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,480
That's so funny.

159
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,280
So funny.

160
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:01,020
(Smile)

161
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,640
Happily heading home.

162
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,840
We had another great day.

163
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:10,380
(Yu Yang & Liang Renfang Mutual Date)

164
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,080
Today has been absolutely

165
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,280
magical.

166
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,000
Yeah.

167
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,640
And what's amazing is that

168
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,600
it rained the day before,
and even the day before that.

169
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:20,880
But today...

170
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,600
The skies just happened to clear up.

171
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,240
A sunny day.

172
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,880
Everything worked out perfectly.

173
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:27,140
(Smiles)

174
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:31,560
(Concerned)
How is it?

175
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:31,880
So good.

176
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:32,440
Is it spicy?

177
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,040
It's really good.

178
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:33,840
You can handle it?

179
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:35,860
It's really good.

180
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:37,060
(Nods)

181
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:38,400
It's so good.

182
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,840
So you like this kind of food.

183
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,680
It feels like a holiday today.

184
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,120
We went to an amusement park,

185
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,680
and now we're eating all this good food.

186
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:48,080
Seriously.

187
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:50,080
It kind of takes me back to
when I was a kid.

188
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,160
When you were a kid.

189
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:53,920
I actually noticed earlier.

190
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,040
When you were dancing, you seemed so...

191
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,400
But I was just messing around.

192
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,440
Yeah, I know you were just having fun.

193
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,220
But you seemed different.

194
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:02,580
(Different)

195
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:04,560
Really.

196
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,000
When I dance, I feel like

197
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,240
I'm being myself.

198
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,960
I feel like

199
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,400
I'm "on fire".

200
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,760
It's just so much fun.

201
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:16,160
Yeah.

202
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,280
So when you feel like dancing,

203
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,920
do you ever go somewhere by yourself?

204
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,560
Like...

205
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,960
When I'm at home, I just start dancing.

206
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:23,920
So you just start dancing?

207
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,120
As long as there's a glass

208
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:28,160
that I can see my reflection in,

209
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,000
I'll probably start dancing.

210
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:34,120
What kind of songs are you best at?

211
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,080
You mean the dizi?

212
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:37,880
Dizi.

213
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,720
With the dizi, I can probably play
pretty much anything.

214
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,760
Yeah.

215
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:43,480
My neighbor's grandpa

216
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,000
basically watched me grow up.

217
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,680
He's such a funny guy.

218
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,440
He'd play the dizi
when he came to pick me up from school.

219
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:50,320
Then we'd walk home through the park,

220
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,400
and he'd play the dizi

221
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,800
just to tease me and make me laugh.

222
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,200
So I...

223
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,680
So he was your first teacher?

224
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:58,400
Yeah, I think he was my first teacher.

225
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,480
That must have meant a lot to you.

226
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,440
Yeah, it did.

227
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,000
It meant a lot to you.

228
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:05,320
He just liked teaching himself.

229
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,240
Instruments.

230
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,600
The xiao [*flute], erhu,
and things like that.

231
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,680
He learned them all on his own.

232
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:10,800
Yeah.

233
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:12,440
Now that you mention it,

234
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,480
I think my grandpa

235
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,280
also played a part
in my artistic upbringing.

236
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:16,640
Really?

237
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:17,720
My grandpa played the erhu.

238
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,920
And my mom studied singing.

239
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:22,440
Yeah.

240
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:25,000
But compared to them,

241
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,600
I don't think
I'm nearly as good at singing. Yeah.

242
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,320
I still prefer dancing.

243
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,640
Your family really has
a strong artistic side.

244
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:34,400
- It's all about the artistic atmosphere.
- Well, not quite that artistic.

245
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,960
We're just a family
that really enjoys the arts.

246
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,160
And whenever there's a holiday

247
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,720
or family celebration,

248
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,680
my dad always asks me to dance.

249
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:46,200
He still does it to this day.

250
00:08:46,780 --> 00:08:49,380
(Smiles)

251
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,680
There's no escaping it.

252
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:51,600
No escaping it.

253
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,040
That talent show I can never escape.

254
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,840
Ever since I was a kid.

255
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:54,680
Same here.

256
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,720
You can't escape the talent show.

257
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,040
I have to play the dizi for everyone.

258
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,680
Maybe we can perform together sometime.

259
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:02,640
Sure.

260
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:08,440
There's still plenty of opportunities.

261
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,960
Okay.

262
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,040
What does this step mean?

263
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,400
First, press this.

264
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,880
Then open it.

265
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:30,200
Put it in.

266
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:33,720
Then the third step is to snap it shut.

267
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,960
The fourth step is...

268
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:35,920
What is this?

269
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,100
I don't know.

270
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:39,340
(Smiles)

271
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:42,400
I think we need an expert.

272
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,240
Anyway, I already snapped it shut.

273
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,120
There, it came out.

274
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,280
Oh, right.

275
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,320
Yeah, and then

276
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,320
the blank shot came out.

277
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,200
So we can start
taking photos now, right?

278
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,160
Let me try.

279
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,840
I'm so nervous.

280
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:02,800
We might waste film.

281
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:03,400
- Does it...
- No, that's not it.

282
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,280
Does it have power?

283
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,080
Yeah.

284
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,560
Your blanket.

285
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:09,220
(Thoughtful)
It's gonna get dirty.

286
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:10,600
I'll hold it.

287
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,520
Let me think about this.

288
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,720
I think the first one
is still a blank shot.

289
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,680
Why?

290
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,080
Because the first one...

291
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,400
Because it came as a whole pack of film.

292
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,600
The first one is always a blank shot.

293
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,800
It's there to protect the film.

294
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,840
But that one already came out.

295
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:29,440
Let me try.

296
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:30,840
Look.

297
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,040
(Cooperating)
Three, two, one.

298
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:37,280
See? The first blank shot came out.

299
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,200
How do you know it's a blank shot?

300
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:41,600
What's this?

301
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,720
This should retract on its own.

302
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:45,960
Right?

303
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,200
Is it a blank shot?

304
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,520
I don't know.

305
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,040
Maybe not.

306
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,920
Why do I feel like it isn't?

307
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,560
This is hilarious.

308
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,680
Let's keep it. It looks cool.

309
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,840
I never would've expected

310
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,920
to get a shot like this.

311
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,440
Isn't it good?

312
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,120
This frame.

313
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,840
Well, anything you take looks good.

314
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,360
Anything you take looks good.

315
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:16,680
Let's go.

316
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:17,240
Okay.

317
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,360
Have you played this before?

318
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,200
No, I haven't.

319
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,320
Let's try it first.

320
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,280
I'll give it a try.

321
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:27,300
(Indoor rock climbing)

322
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,080
Be careful.

323
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,040
Where are you going, Liang Xiaoyu?

324
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:36,640
I'm just trying to go up.

325
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,120
Oh, go up.

326
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,520
I thought she was going up on the right.

327
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,760
Can you only grip that one
with your fingers?

328
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,360
I can't get a grip on this one.

329
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,120
Can you use it for leverage?

330
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:48,760
I can't reach it.

331
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,360
Can you grab the green one?

332
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:56,560
I think you can.

333
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:58,680
Yeah, I can.

334
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,000
And there's nowhere else to step.

335
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,720
Put your left foot

336
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,400
on the white hold on your left.

337
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:07,880
Yeah.

338
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,080
You can't really grip that one.

339
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,560
That one's really hard.

340
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:12,520
This isn't working.

341
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,080
Then use your left hand

342
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,880
to grab the pink one.

343
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,240
I can't hold onto the pink one.

344
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:17,000
I'm done.

345
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,440
I think I'll stay out of the way.

346
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,560
Can you put your left foot...

347
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,120
Put your left foot on the hold
to your left.

348
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,320
Yeah, right there.

349
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,280
I can't get past this.

350
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:26,520
Yeah, this part is pretty hard
to get through.

351
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:29,320
Put your right foot

352
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,320
on the yellow hold in the middle.

353
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,080
You can reach it, right? Yeah.

354
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,280
And then?

355
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:34,920
Then

356
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,280
use your right foot to push off.

357
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,400
Then put your left foot

358
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,360
on the white hold on your left.

359
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,680
Be careful.

360
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:44,000
This move is way too difficult.

361
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,640
I feel like Liang Xiaoyu's

362
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,480
position right now

363
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:47,960
is kind of awkward.

364
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:51,040
Whoa!

365
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,080
- That's amazing!
- Oh my God!

366
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:53,240
Forget it.

367
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,480
Let's not make it too hard.

368
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,440
Just turn around
and you can reach the bell.

369
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:58,760
Turn around.

370
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,320
You did it.

371
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:03,160
Wait.

372
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:03,960
You took off the spring rope.

373
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:06,760
Wait.

374
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,680
You need to hook it back on.

375
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,040
I can't get it on.

376
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,000
Seriously, I can't get it on.

377
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,160
Just take it down.

378
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,200
That actually took a lot of energy.

379
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,120
Here we go.

380
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,120
Jump!

381
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:23,720
Thank you, everyone.

382
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,320
That was awesome.

383
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,080
That was amazing.

384
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:28,040
Should we find that spring rope first?

385
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:28,600
I'll look for it.

386
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,400
It's right there.

387
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:31,640
I know. I think it's over here.

388
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:32,320
I just saw it.

389
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,200
Sun Bohan,

390
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:36,760
when you go up there,

391
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:38,680
hook that spring rope onto it.

392
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:39,440
Where's it?

393
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:39,800
Here.

394
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,440
Throw it over.

395
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:41,520
Be careful.

396
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,200
It has one...

397
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,640
That loop is kind of weird.

398
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:45,960
Thanks for doing that.

399
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,400
It has a hole.

400
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:51,800
You can thread it through,
but it's really hard.

401
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,800
I don't think I can get it hooked.

402
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:53,880
Any hole you can thread it through
will work.

403
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:54,800
I think you can do it.

404
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,920
If I can hook it on, I'll do it.

405
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:13,440
Move sideways.

406
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,000
Let me see.

407
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,100
(Pulling out the spring rope)

408
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:21,360
He's taking it out of his pocket.

409
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,520
Be careful.

410
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,320
Okay.

411
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,440
He's Spider-Man.

412
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,000
Let's take a picture.

413
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,760
Three, two, one.

414
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,080
So handsome.

415
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,600
Handsome.

416
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,480
"Sculpture".

417
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:39,960
Okay, it's hooked.

418
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,440
Let's go. Let's head back.

419
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:43,240
Okay.

420
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,560
Do you want to sit for a bit?

421
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,360
Sure.

422
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:48,520
This photo didn't come out.

423
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,400
Maybe that's just how it is.

424
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,480
Yeah, I guess that's how it turned out.

425
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,320
(Turns around)
Go.

426
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,080
After you.

427
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,320
Rock, paper, scissors.

428
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:00,440
You win.

429
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,320
(Thinking)

430
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:02,000
You won this round.

431
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:02,680
No, the loser...

432
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,400
The loser goes first.

433
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,240
The one who loses goes first?

434
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,680
Because we both want to go last.

435
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:07,120
Okay.

436
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,320
Then I'll go first.

437
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,000
Sit. Let's get a massage for a bit.

438
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:22,420
(Glances)

439
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,280
Here's one for you.

440
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,920
(Hands it over)
This color suits you better.

441
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:29,720
Thanks.

442
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,840
Do you ever come out
for a massage at night?

443
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:33,640
No.

444
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,520
But if you can't sleep at night,

445
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:37,040
you could get a massage or something.

446
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:38,040
Everyone's asleep.

447
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,480
I feel like I'd disturb everyone.

448
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,600
There's even a rocking chair
to help you sleep.

449
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:45,480
Are you getting sleepy now?

450
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:46,720
I'm okay.

451
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,800
It can heat up too.

452
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,000
So are you going to the hospital
tomorrow morning

453
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,960
or going to work?

454
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:57,080
I'll probably go to the hospital first.

455
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:58,760
Then go to work.

456
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,080
Yeah.

457
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,280
Do you ever make little cakes
for yourselves?

458
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:04,920
No.

459
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,120
But I saw there's an oven here.

460
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:08,480
We could actually bake
some cookies or something.

461
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,160
But I took a look at it today,

462
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,400
and it seems a little complicated.

463
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,920
A little complicated?

464
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,800
Think about what we haven't had lately.

465
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,880
We can make
something different tomorrow.

466
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:24,320
Then you think about it.

467
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,480
You think about what you want to eat.

468
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,320
Oh, I think?

469
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,520
Are you coming back early
or late tomorrow?

470
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,920
I'm not really sure.

471
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,100
What time will you be back?

472
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:36,100
(Turns to look)

473
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,560
Maybe seven or eight.

474
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:40,380
(Glances)

475
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,320
Do you feel like you've

476
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:44,480
completely gotten used to life
at Signal House?

477
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,720
Pretty much.

478
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,680
Cooking every day

479
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:51,320
and making sure you guys eat well
is pretty satisfying.

480
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:52,900
(Glances)

481
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:54,900
(Smiles)

482
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:59,240
Do you get enough to eat
at the hospital?

483
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,440
(Concerned)
I do.

484
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,520
Yeah, I even had
a salted egg yolk cake today.

485
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:06,840
Okay.

486
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:11,080
If you ever feel really tired

487
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,840
or have a lot on your mind,

488
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:14,320
you can talk to me.

489
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:17,800
You can just treat here as a place

490
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:21,000
where I listen to you vent.

491
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,600
Okay.

492
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:25,800
You too.

493
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:27,920
I'm okay.

494
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,800
I don't really have anything
bothering me right now.

495
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:32,500
Is anything bothering you right now?

496
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,480
(Turns to look)

497
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:35,080
Not too much.

498
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:35,960
So there's still

499
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:36,920
a little.

500
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:38,640
Talk to me.

501
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:41,560
I've been pretty happy
these past few days.

502
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:43,080
But you're still

503
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:44,440
worried about Xing,

504
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,240
right?

505
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,440
Yeah, it all happened so suddenly.

506
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,880
But I can see that she's getting better.

507
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:52,160
Yeah, she's definitely improving.

508
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,480
Actually, that night at the hospital,

509
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,440
I saw Sun Bohan crying.

510
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,360
I didn't expect the feelings

511
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:02,360
to hit me that hard.

512
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,200
I was completely swept up in it.

513
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,400
Actually,

514
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,440
from Xing's perspective,

515
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:09,000
I think it was fate.

516
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,280
She actually told me today

517
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,760
that she's glad she used the coin.

518
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:12,560
Otherwise,

519
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,360
she and Sun Bohan might not have
gotten this close.

520
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:16,080
Yeah.

521
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,480
You didn't hesitate

522
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:18,760
to pick Sun Bohan for her, did you?

523
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:19,840
I didn't hesitate for a second.

524
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:20,680
I think she would've

525
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,560
picked Sun Bohan too if she'd
gotten here first.

526
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:26,360
I also told Xing

527
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:27,640
that we went
to the supermarket together.

528
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,480
And the four of us
should go together sometime.

529
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:32,800
Sure.

530
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,000
We can shop together.

531
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:37,400
Sure.

532
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,400
Is there anything else

533
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,160
you still want to do

534
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,800
but haven't gotten around to?

535
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:44,000
Definitely.

536
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:45,720
What about you?

537
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:52,280
For me, I think I'd really like

538
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,120
for us to get another chance

539
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:55,160
to go out together.

540
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:57,640
I feel like
it was a little disappointing last time.

541
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,240
It was pretty nice, though.

542
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,600
We got to see such a beautiful sunset.

543
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,440
Yeah, that was the best part
at the very end.

544
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:11,820
(Exchanging glances)

545
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,600
What's this? There's so much.

546
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:20,080
It's what they made.

547
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,160
Singapore-style rice noodles.

548
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,320
Looks really good.

549
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,240
What's up?

550
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:25,960
Singapore-style shrimp.

551
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:27,240
Let's go upstairs.

552
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:28,280
Me?

553
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:29,120
Let's go.

554
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,160
What's up?

555
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,120
Did you get me a gift?

556
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:40,600
So happy.

557
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,280
What kind of gift is it?

558
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:46,280
It's this.

559
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:46,840
Yeah.

560
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,760
Don't say anything yet.

561
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:49,880
Here you go.

562
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:51,680
Wait.

563
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,200
Let me think about how to put this.

564
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:54,960
Because you're

565
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,000
(Suddenly serious)
studying medicine,

566
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,400
so you probably wash your hands a lot.

567
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,280
So I got you something

568
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:00,760
to help protect your hands.

569
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,080
I love it.

570
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:05,920
Even though I haven't seen it yet.

571
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,120
Let's open it.

572
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:10,480
